Theorem RL-30: Effect-based call annotations

  Preconditions:
    - Effect-based call annotations per Annex E §AIMS RL-30
    - Parameter access from IC-3 ParamContract.access + may_share
    - Borrowed + may_share=false: reads only; Borrowed + may_share=true: reads+RC-header writes; Owned: reads+writes
    - Pure calls -> memory(none); may_share=true -> memory(... inaccessiblemem: readwrite); etc.

  Soundness property:
    Forall function f, call site c.
      RL-30 emits LLVM memory(...) attribute on c
      consistent with derived IC-5 + ParamContract:
        pure read-only: memory(argmem: read)
        pure + may_read_inaccessible: memory(argmem: read, inaccessiblemem: read)
        pure all-Absent params: memory(none)
        allocating + arg access: memory(argmem: readwrite, inaccessiblemem: readwrite)
        pure allocator (no arg access): memory(inaccessiblemem: readwrite)
        may_share=true + Borrowed: memory(argmem: read, inaccessiblemem: readwrite)
        may_share=true + no params: memory(inaccessiblemem: readwrite)
        deallocating: memory(inaccessiblemem: readwrite) (+argmem if Owned/may_share)
        non-allocating Owned-param writers: memory(argmem: readwrite, inaccessiblemem: readwrite)
        fallback: memory(argmem: readwrite, inaccessiblemem: readwrite).

  Proof obligation:
    sorry -- discharged by sec-08 realization rule proofs

    Engines dispatched:
      rc_counting
      refinement
      case_analysis

  Expected:
    status: unimplemented_engine_shape
    reason: sec-01 skeleton; sec-08 discharges RL-30 effect-based call annotations

