Theorem RL-34: Tail call preservation

  Preconditions:
    - Tail call preservation per Annex E §AIMS RL-34
    - Never insert RcDec after a tail call
    - Transfer ownership ONLY when callee parameter is Owned
    - Callee Borrowed: tail-call requires caller to arrange dec BEFORE call

  Soundness property:
    Forall function f, tail call c with arg v to callee parameter p.
      p.access = O implies tail call permitted; ownership of v transfers to callee (no caller-side dec)
      p.access = Borrowed implies tail-call requires caller arranges RcDec(v) BEFORE c (no post-tail-call dec).

